  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+25\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $25$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}}_{\u23df}-{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}+25\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}+25\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
